A new Atelier app scaffolded by `atelier init` (Sprint 1.1 standalone mode).

## Getting started

```bash
pnpm install         # already done if you used `--install`
pnpm dev             # boots `atelier vault dev` (port 4001) + `next dev` (port 3000)
```

Open <http://localhost:3000>.

For local development, first copy the env example:

```bash
cp .env.local.example .env.local
# Optional: drop a Gemini key in if you have one
```

Without a Gemini key, the deterministic `GenericFallbackCompiler` ships
hand-written manifests so the page still renders.

## Layout

- `app/` — Next.js 15 App Router routes.
  - `app/api/cir/manifest/[...slug]/` — the manifest API the runtime fetches.
  - `app/api/triggers/publish/` — POST a trigger payload to broadcast it via SSE.
- `lib/atelier-server.ts` — the canonical server-side wiring (compiler +
  cache + audit + resolvers). Customise this to swap in your own data
  resolvers or capability set.
- `recipes/` — JSON recipes the LLM compiler uses as exemplars.
- `policies/` — JSON policy artifacts. Layered on top of the baseline policies.
- `capabilities/` — capability JSON artifacts. Where you declare what the
  agent is allowed to read / mutate.
- `skills/` — markdown skill bundles that nudge the compiler's prose.
- `brand-kit.json` — design tokens, voice, accessibility minimums.

